        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAs">III As</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="III As. Inscr." corresp="#wit-q">Decretum episcoporum et aliorum sapientum de Kantia de pace obseruanda.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-q">Decretum episcoporum et aliorum sapientum de Kantia de pace observanda.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-q">The decree of the bishops and other councillors in Kent, concerning measures for the preservation of public peace.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only (Quadripartitus); Liebermann prints no German translation. Liebermann's text is from K (Cotton Domitian A VIII?) compared with Co, Or, Jl (Julius C II), T and the group MHkBr. ‘Litera missa regi Adelstano per episcopos et alios dominos Kancie’ is written in red at the foot of the page in T.</note>
      </div>
